EVALUATION.md §3.4, §9.3 step 3 (review call a): while an amended record re-derives its defaults,
the refs it holds into an enclosing instance's collection are unbound, as when it is first
built: `config` is poisoned by the same E3505 as `written` (no enclosing Config).
-- layers --
dev
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// Tier.
record Tier {
  /// Weight.
  weight: Int = 1
}

/// Server.
record Server {
  /// Pick.
  pick: ref Tier = low
  /// X.
  x: Int = 0
  /// W.
  w: Int = if x > 0 { pick.weight } else { 0 }
}

/// Config.
record Config {
  /// Tiers.
  tiers: table Tier = { low { weight: 3 } }
  /// Server.
  server: Server = {}
}

/// Amended.
let config: Config = {}

/// Written.
let written: Config = { server: { x: 1 } }
-- a/dev.canon --
package a
layer dev

amend config {
  server.x: 1
}
-- dump.txt --
a.config poisoned
a.written poisoned

error[E3505]  a/a.canon:17:23
  ref Tier has no enclosing Config to resolve against

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
